Place all files inside a single folder  - to run enter qemu-system-i386 -cdrom 511OS.iso in terminal\
\
Kernel folder - kernel.cpp is main kernel code\
\
WHEN CHANGING KERNEL.CPP\
COPY AND PASTE FOLLOWING CODE INSIDE TERMINAL WITH 511OS FOLDER OPEN IN TERMINAL\
\
nasm -f elf32 boot/boot.asm -o boot.o\
i686-elf-g++ -m32 -ffreestanding -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti -c kernel/kernel.cpp -o kernel.o\
i686-elf-g++ -m32 -T linker.ld -ffreestanding -nostdlib -o kernel.elf boot.o kernel.o -lgcc\
cp kernel.elf iso/boot/kernel.elf\
i686-elf-grub-mkrescue -o 511OS.iso iso\
qemu-system-i386 -cdrom 511OS.iso\
\
This recompiles the code so it updates the changes\
\
(Will work on getting a script to run so we don't have to enter this every time)\
(For windows it might work differently)}
